Process
-------

What is a process ?

A program which is under execution is called process. 

./a.out -> process running in foreground
./a.out& -> process running in background

when a process started execution process manager will provide the unique id called as pid.

Daemon process : A Daemon process is special process that is created and handled by the system in the same way as other process.
		 Daemon process will start running once system booting completed, they terminate when system shutdown.
		 Many services are started as daemons.

		 fg will bring background process to foreground
		 fg jobid -> according to jobid particular process is getback a foreground

Multiprocessing
---------------

1. Hardware multiprocessing
	
	in case of hardware multiprocessing for every application, seperate hardware (CPU) is presented.

2. Software multiprocessing
	
	in case of software multiprocessing all applications will run on a single CPU with help of OS.
	


/proc/sys/kernel/pid_max -> pid max range 

4194304 -> for my system

pid for my system ranges from 0 to 4194304

0 -> scheduler
1 -> init process

once pid values reaches pid max range again will start from 300 before 300 many numbers are reserved. 

During the life of a process it may enter into different states.

State of process
----------------

-> Ready state
-> Running state
-> Wait state
-> Delay state
-> Suspended state


Ready state
-----------

	If the process is in ready state it needs CPU but nothing. Once it dispatched to CPU then it is in running state.

Running state
-------------

	Process is executed by CPU.

Wait state
----------

	waiting for an external event to finish. 
	let us consider scanf(). 

	new process ---------> ready ---------> Running
                     admitted        dispatcher

	during run time if it waiting for external events then it goes to wait state and if events completed then it goes to ready state. when the cpu is completed other tasks then again dispatcher dispatches to running state. 



Delayed State
-------------
	
	process intentionally goes to delay state (by providing sleep()). 

new -> ready --------------> CPU  
	^	dispatcher    |
	|		      |
	| delay complted		  
	|		     delay
	______________________|



dispatcher is a module in process manager it gives control of the CPU to the process.



Suspended State 
---------------

During the life of a process it is possible to suspend the process by sending signal.

kill -19 process_id for suspend the process
kill -18 process_id for resume the process
			
			dispatcher
new ---------> ready  --------------->  (p1) CPU
     admitted	  ^			  |
		  | 			  |  kill -19 pid
     kill -18 pid |  resume		  |
		  |_______________________|
